# deep-equal

Deep equality testing for JavaScript objects and arrays.

## Installation

```bash
$ npm i deep-equal --save-dev
```

## Usage

`isEqual` is a fast `===` comparison function that uses `deep-equal` to compare nested objects.
With this in mind, you can use it like so:

```js
console.log(deepEqual(0, 0)); //=> true
console.log(isEqual({a: 1}, {a: 2})); //=> false
```

The options are the same as those listed in [`deep-equal`](https://github.com/chriso/deep-equal), but they are not supported by default because of performance concerns. To enable them, set the environment variable `DEEP_EQUAL_OPTIONS` to the desired key-value pairs separated by commas:

```sh
$ DEEP_EQUAL_OPTIONS=relaxed,isFlat=true node test/equality.test.js
```

### Example

```js
// Custom polyfill for Array.isArray
if (!Array.isArray)
	Array.isArray = function(arg) { return Object.prototype.toString.call(arg) == '[object Array]' };

require('deep-equal').options({ relaxed: true });
deepEqual([{}, {}], [{}, {}]); //=> true
deepEqual([{a: 1}], [{a: 1}]); //=> true
```
